    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 661301455515648
    m_Localized: "The entire ecosystem depends on this fish. It is very common and
      found in every biome. It is relatively fast but also quite weak. It\u2019s
      a great food source for early-game progression."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 661422603792384
    m_Localized: "In the beginning was the word, then the crab appeared, and then
      the whole world was created around it. Slow, nutritious, defenseless, but soooo
      delicious\u2014the player\u2019s best friend."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 661465922564096
    m_Localized: "A small, agile, and rather slow fish found in the crevices of coral
      reefs and at the edges of seaweed forests. It has bright coloring, but this
      only plays into the hands of its predators. It\u2019s best not to be this fish
      for long."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 661505349021696
    m_Localized: "The very first serious predator in the game. Its elongated body
      and camouflage allow it to hunt more effectively in open bodies of water. However,
      nature has not endowed this predator with much intelligence. It\u2019s easy
      to outwit it while fleeing beneath boulders. The fish that everyone loves the
      most in the hardest game mode."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 661536483340288
    m_Localized: "One of the slowest, longest, and most yellowish fish. Controlling
      a fish like this is like piloting an airplane with your eyes closed. It\u2019s
      most commonly found in seaweed forests. It has a wide bite radius, which can
      help it quickly devour objects around it."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 661567122731008
    m_Localized: "A true silent killer. A small, fast, and highly agile fish with
      a relatively short lifespan. A very dangerous fish\u2014whoever controls it
      controls half the ocean. Nature has endowed it with venom and immunity to it,
      but this game isn\u2019t nature."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 661598261243904
    m_Localized: A quiet, slow-moving tank, but one capable of piercing armor. No
      matter how fast or how far the Pterois flees, sooner or later this predator
      will catch up to it and devour it. It often swims through rocky gorges and
      prefers solitude.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 661625301921792
    m_Localized: "The fastest and one of the most dangerous predators. It\u2019s
      very unpredictable\u2014by the time you\u2019re figuring out how to escape,
      it\u2019ll already be finishing off your remains. It\u2019s recommended to
      keep an eye out for shadows on the underwater surface so you can escape before
      it spots you."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 661637779976192
    m_Localized: "A half-hearted attempt to join the shark class. It\u2019s a threat
      to the entire food chain\u2014worse than itself. On the other hand, for this
      fish, dying at the hands of one of its own kind is a common occurrence. It
      is found in deep-sea coral and water lily biomes."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 661729958195200
    m_Localized: It is the second most dangerous shark in its class. Fast, aggressive,
      and nearly invisible. When it spots a poisonous jellyfish, this shark will
      charge without hesitation. It eats almost everything it sees; sometimes this
      is a fatal choice, but thanks to that choice, it is still alive.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 661748178251776
    m_Localized: "If there is a manifestation of boundless power in the depths of
      the ocean, it is right before you. An invincible predator\u2014heavy, massive,
      bloodthirsty, and almost white. As the apex predator in the game\u2019s food
      chain, it can grow to an extraordinarily large size compared to all other sharks.
      Its growth knows no bounds. If you\u2019ve spotted it, there\u2019s no point
      in running anymore."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 661763097391104
    m_Localized: "What\u2019s that annoying whistling sound? That\u2019s right! It\u2019s
      an almost indestructible inflatable ball covered in spikes on all sides. It\u2019s
      fast, annoying, but looooves hugs\u2014if you do too, it\u2019s waiting for
      you. You\u2019ll find it in every biome in the game. As it inflates, the damage
      from its spikes increases."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 661777437716480
    m_Localized: A cephalopod whose presence here is a mystery. It is found exclusively
      in the deep-sea coral biome, though it occasionally ventures beyond its boundaries.
      When danger approaches, it releases toxic ink into the water. When it approaches
      certain large, colorful objects, it changes the color of its camouflage.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 683583313833984
    m_Localized: Research Biome
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 684106687475712
    m_Localized: Boost Research \n(-15m)
